A||||13||Ferrari_cdn||CRAPPY running when cold, HELP!||||5||
Z||000000||Ferrari_cdn||11-24-2001||03:43 AM||||My Fiero runs like crap when it is cold.  I've done some tuning up, like replacing spark plugs, fuel filter and 02 sensor.  Mach10 says that I am running rich.  (I run through a complete tank within 280 kms.  Thats only a little bit longer than V6s.  When cold, and if I try to be heavy on the accelerator in first and in low rpms, she wouldn't accelerate for a few seconds, then she'll jump forward.  She'll stop accelerating very quickly and then do the cycle all over again.  (sorta like riding a bronco) She will smooth out when I'm higher in rpms.  When I shift to second and engage, then once I hit the gas, it's like a sledgehammer hit me from behind.   Not a smooth ride.  After a few minutes and once warmed up, she runs damn smooth.<P>Maybe she's running too cold?  I look at my water temp and after a few minutes, it is always at the 1/4 mark.  A little bit past the 1/4 mark when under load and when idling, she will creep past the 1/4 mark towards the cold side.  After a long while, the grills on my '84 is not hot to the touch.<P>Mach and I can't seem to figure out the problem.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ferrari_cdn" TARGET=_blank>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ferrari_cdn.JPG">   </A>  <BR>AIM: CanadianFiero<p>[This message has been edited by Ferrari_cdn (edited 11-24-2001).]||||reg||5
